  step,dige:46ec288dbaeec02c
  step=2,dige:2e07aacb8c0f5d96
  step=3,dige:25eceda189879ca3
    Assertion:friends,sentence:Alice and Bob become friends — each Pier carries a Music grant the other signed — a real account to persist
  step=4,dige:701c68a2f13b914e
    Assertion:account-alone,sentence:the account persists to disk — its snap carries the friendship grant and the keypair inline so the owner-local backup stands alone
    Assertion:roster-pub-only,sentence:the roster names its owner for recognition — pub and friendly on disk and never the private key
  step=5,dige:ecd9ebcc1b88d998
    Assertion:reseed-reborn,sentence:a fresh browser reseeds its owner off disk — the friendship and the private key reborn from the account snap alone
    Assertion:reseed-signs,sentence:the reseeded key still signs — a new grant minted after the disk round trip verifies under the same public key
    Assertion:reseed-identical,sentence:the account survives the disk round trip byte for byte — the reseeded self re-saves to the very same snap
  step=6,dige:1104cd13b30596dc
    Assertion:two-owners,sentence:two owners share the one FSA point — enumeration finds both accounts on disk keyed by prepub
    Assertion:named-pick,sentence:the requested owner is the one reseeded — a named pick lands Carol not merely the first account and her own key thaws
    Assertion:roster-both,sentence:the roster names both owners for recognition — each pub and friendly on disk and neither private key
  step=7,dige:c7f55cfe63d35614
    Assertion:update-not-append,sentence:the account write-through is an update not an append — a revocation re-saves the whole snap so disk tracks the live account
    Assertion:tombstone-survives,sentence:a revocation survives the disk round trip — the reseeded account carries the NotGrant tombstone so a reload never silently re-grants
